use Kreait\Firebase\Factory;
use Kreait\Firebase\Auth;

$factory = (new Factory)
    ->withServiceAccount('path/to/serviceAccountKey.json')
    ->withDatabaseUri('https://your-database-name.firebaseio.com');

$auth = $factory->createAuth();
Once you have the Auth instance, you can generate a custom token for a guest user. The generateCustomToken method requires a user identifier (UID) and optionally a custom claims object. For a guest user, you can generate a random UID and use it to create the token:
$uid = 'guest-' . uniqid(); // Generate a unique ID for the guest user
$token = $auth->generateCustomToken($uid);
This token can then be sent to the client, where it can be used to sign in the user using Firebase's signInWithCustomToken method.
On the client side (e.g., using Firebase JavaScript SDK), you can sign in with the custom token like this:
firebase.auth().signInWithCustomToken(token)
    .then(function(userCredential) {
        // Signed in
        var user = userCredential.user;
        // ...
    })
    .catch(function(error) {
        // Handle error
    });
Note that the custom token is valid for a limited time (usually 1 hour), and it's meant to be used once. Also, you should ensure that your Firebase project is configured to allow custom token authentication.
